# Tersoff silicon-carbon, J. Tersoff, Phys. Rev. B 39, 5566 (1989), with the
# erratum Phys. Rev. B 41, 3248 (1990): carbon B = 346.74 eV, d = 4.3484.
# LAMMPS pair_style tersoff format, metal units. These are the constants
# of rgpot::TersoffSiC. Mixed pairs follow the 1989 rules: lambda1 and
# lambda2 arithmetic means, A geometric, B = chi * geometric with
# chi = 0.9776, and the inner and outer cutoffs (R - D and R + D here)
# geometric means of the elements' own. The LAMMPS potentials/SiC.tersoff
# file omits the erratum, uses Si lambda2 = 1.73222 and rounds the mixed
# taper to R = 2.36, D = 0.15.
# tests/python/test_lammps_agreement.py checks every value against
# TersoffSiC().params().
